 trust do you think that  we should be government should be  allowed to collect this data do they  need it well i think i mean i personally  do think that there is data there that  actually you know is is important why  why well because because increasingly  you know um people uh the way you  actually actually get to know and able  to intercept and stop because this is  the problem you know in the past we used  to have crime of a kind you know well  you could deal with people after they've  done something we now have potentially  such horrendous crimes around including  including terrorism and long-stale  long-organized crime where actually the  name of the game is disrupt people and  prevent them actually doing it the only  way you can do that is getting hold of  information you know before they  actually act so you do have to they  communicate on the internet and they  communicate in on social media you've  got to be able no to to be able to  penetrate that but  you know for your my safeguard we need  to know that that's only being done in a  lawful way all only being done  proportionately only being done  necessarily and that i think is what  david anderson is really getting at  let's have a system that really commands  confidence and he is transferring  certain paths to the courts for that  what's your view on the recommendation  to strip ministers of their power to  issue interception warrants and give it  to judges because the prime minister  spokesman's always suggested this could  be problematic do you think well  you can perfectly well you can perfectly  well make a case for for it continuing  to be an act that  that is a political act  um  david anderson has come down on the side  of judges doing it now i would say i  actually support that why do i support  that not because i think that ministers  have abused their powers but i do think  that in the current climate it's very  important to command confidence and i  think that will increase the people's  confidence in the you know in that this  is a properly regulated system he also  said in his report that the agency's  capabilities should be made more public  as in we should know more about what  they do and how they operate obviously  that's going to then give information  out there to people we don't necessarily  want to have that information well then  they can evade the authorities i don't  think he's saying  they should make their operations public  what do you expect  about their activities well up to a  point yes um but i mean there comes a  point where how you're doing it is  actually an operation uh but but people  said that people should be able to  understand what these paths consist of  and what they're used for and why they  are necessary i think all of that does  is there going to be a danger though  and and snowden you know really has made  that necessary  and so yeah i do now i support all that  i think that i think that all of that's  a good idea and i think you know it's  not i'm not a good idea for for  authority to duck the issue uh we do we  do need actually to have this debate  okay neville jones thank you very much  for your thoughts thank you

